# FIG-09-02: Two representations, two costs
status: draft   rev: 1   date: 2026-10-22   author: illustration-spec agent

## 1. Summary

The sheet holds the sample graph twice: as an adjacency list with five key rows, and as a five by five adjacency matrix, with a bottom strip setting the two containers against each other on space and on query. The matrix is drawn largest, because its empty cells are the argument: on the whole sample graph the list stores 16 entries, the table holds 64 cells, and 48 of those cells record no edge.

MESSAGE = the list pays for the edges that exist, the matrix pays for every pair, and the one cell join test is bought with cells that hold nothing.

## 2. Communicative intent

- AUDIENCE: a student revising for an exam, who can read pseudocode, has met stacks, queues and heaps in chapters 4 and 5, and has read section 9.1.1 once.
- INTENDED CHANGE: from "two ways to store a graph, pick either" to "each container is a cost curve, and the matrix's cost is quadratic in a quantity the edges never use".
- READING CONTEXT: inside chapter 9 after the 9.1.1 paragraph that ends "beside the decompositions that use them", in a column capped at 1120 px, light and dark, phone read in the site lightbox at 2x zoom.
- REPRODUCTION: 1000 unit flat schematic at 1000 by 660, rebuilt from the inventory in section 6, no external asset and no photograph.
- LIFETIME: illustration system for the chapter
- ASSUMPTIONS: 1. The cost pair counts the whole sample graph, V 8 and E 8, so 16 entries against 64 cells; the arithmetic comes from the task brief and is fixed once in section 6. 2. Views A and B draw the five vertex connected piece, as the roster row of PLAN.md states. 3. O(V+E), O(V squared) and the O(1) join test are chapter 9.1.1; the list answering a join test by scanning one row is derived from the adjacency list definition and is logged in section 4. 4. Type sizes are the chapter's, nothing below 14 canvas units. 5. The 1000 vertex graph of exercise 2 is out of scope, as PLAN.md open question 2 decides.

## 3. Goals and non-goals

- GOAL-1 The reader can count the list's 16 entries and the matrix's 64 cells on the sheet and see that both counts describe the same eight vertex graph.
- GOAL-2 The reader can point at one filled cell and at its mirror and say that the same edge is stored twice, once in each half.
- GOAL-3 The reader can say which container answers a join test in one cell and which must scan a row.
- NON-GOAL-1 No traversal state: BFS, DFS and Dijkstra belong to FIG-09-07 to FIG-09-09.
- NON-GOAL-2 No weight is drawn or claimed; weights belong to FIG-09-05 and FIG-09-09.
- NON-GOAL-3 No petgraph family comparison; that argument is a table, not this sheet.
- NON-GOAL-4 No directed graph, so no in-degree and out-degree count appears.

## 4. Constraints

- canvas: viewBox `0 0 1000 660`, aspect 1000:660, three views on one sheet.
- node budget: 380 live nodes, the two panel allowance of BRIEFING section 4 taken as the cap for this three view sheet; the inventory sums to 98.
- palette budget: the palette rows in section 5 are the only paints; no hue is added.
- typography: Montserrat, self hosted; vertex id 18, panel label 16 semibold, value and callout 15, note 14.
- text split: prose stays in the chapter markdown; in-SVG labels are vertex ids, the two counts, the two asymptotes and one to three word notes, 24 characters maximum, 2 lines maximum.
- convention: flat schematic, one sheet, one projection, no perspective and no depth.
- time appetite: half a day for the build and one review pass.
- detail: full
- element floor: 26 in A, 40 in B, 10 in C, read from the inventory in section 6.
- boundaries: this file only; no edit under `content/`, `web/`, `pipeline/`, `data/`, and no other spec.
- coordinates: no vertex is drawn, so the canonical node table of BRIEFING section 3 is not used; the vertex order `s`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `t` is inherited from it, and the three panel boxes are placed here (A 32 to 452, B 500 to 968, strip band 32 to 968).
- claim status: 5 vertices and 6 edges in the piece, degrees s 2, a 4, b 3, c 3, t 2, 8 vertices and 8 edges in the sample graph, 16 entries and 64 cells, all `verified` from BRIEFING section 2.
- claim status: 25 cells (5 times 5) and 14 filled cells (7 edges stored in each half), `derived`, arithmetic stated in section 6.
- claim status: O(V+E) space, O(V squared) space and the O(1) join test are `chapter`, section 9.1.1; the list answering a join test by scanning the row of one endpoint is `derived` from that section's definition, named as the operation, with no complexity asserted for it.

## 5. Visual system lock

- projection: flat schematic, front on, one sheet, no depth, no shadow.
- line grammar: outline 3.2 for panel frames, cells and the inset of a filled cell; connector and leader 1.6; hairline 1.0 for rules and gridlines; long dash 6 4 on the diagonal rule only; no arrowhead, because nothing flows.
- palette: role names only, light hex in `:root`, dark hex in `.dark`, no raw hex inside the drawing.

| NAME | HEX (light) | HEX (dark) | ROLE | USED FOR |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ink | #15181e | #e8eaef | structure and primary text | vertex ids, counts, panel labels |
| muted | #5c6470 | #a3abba | meaningful secondary | leaders, diagonal rule, half labels, notes |
| border | #e7eaf0 | #262b36 | decorative separation | panel frames, row rules, cell rules |
| card | #ffffff | #15181e | panel fill | panel and empty cell background |
| wash | #f5f7fa | #111522 | table zebra | key rows 2 and 4 of the list |
| accent | #1d4ed8 | #7aa2ff | active, examined | filled cell above the diagonal and its mirror |
| accent-soft | #eef3fe | #16213c | active wash | the space column band of the strip |
| accent-ink | #14357f | #c7d6ff | text on accent-soft | the two space values and the two asymptotes |
| success | #157347 | #4ade80 | final, verified | the filled cell count, 12 |

- value plan: three foundation values (card, wash, accent-soft) plus ink as the darkest text value; the strongest junction sits on the boundary between a filled cell and its empty neighbour inside the grid, named in section 8.
- light: flat, no light source declared, no shadow, no gradient.
- detail floor: stroke 1.0 and type 14, nothing below either.
- style reference: the chapter's other sheets and the geometry in BRIEFING section 3; no icon set, no texture.
- hue rule (BRIEFING section 5): faint and border carry no text and no meaningful edge, so the filled against empty distinction is carried by an inset outline and by position, not by fill alone.

## 6. Content inventory

The counted graph, stated once: the cost pair counts the whole sample graph, V 8 and E 8, so V + E = 8 + 8 = 16 entries and V times V = 8 times 8 = 64 cells. Views A and B draw the connected piece, whose grid holds 25 cells and 14 filled cells. The strip's pair is the whole graph, and no other pair appears on the sheet.

